<head>
    <title>Dreego Blog · v3 body md</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Version 3 of the blog index: the whole page written as a Markdown body.">
</head>

<server>
    type Post struct {
        Title   string
        Slug    string
        Date    string
        Excerpt string
    }
    posts := []Post{
        {Title: "Hello, Dreego", Slug: "hello-dreego", Date: "2026-08-24", Excerpt: "A first look at the v0.2 and v0.3 releases: typed SSR, the render foundation, and Markdown bodies."},
        {Title: "The Render Foundation", Slug: "rendering-foundation", Date: "2026-08-18", Excerpt: "How the v0.2 render foundation keeps generated inputs typed and opens the door to SSG and Wails."},
        {Title: "Markdown in the Body", Slug: "markdown-in-the-body", Date: "2026-08-10", Excerpt: "Write real Markdown in a <body lang=\"md\"> section and mix in Dreego constructs."},
        {Title: "Interactive Markdown", Slug: "interactive-markdown", Date: "2026-08-08", Excerpt: "HTMX-powered interactivity inside a Markdown body — components, styles, and scripts coexist."},
    }
</server>

<body lang="md">
<nav class="mb-10 flex items-center gap-2" aria-label="Version switcher">
    <a href="/blog/" class="rounded-full border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100">v1 · HTML</a>
    <a href="/blog/v2" class="rounded-full border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100">v2 · md tag</a>
    <a href="/blog/v3" class="rounded-full bg-slate-950 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white">v3 · body md</a>
</nav>

Field notes

## Building Dreego, in the open.

Short posts about the framework, its design constraints, and the decisions behind each release.

01 / posts

## Latest writing.

Every post is a real Markdown body rendered by the v0.3 md processor.

<div class="cards">
    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        {#each posts as post}
            <@PostCard title={post.Title} slug={post.Slug} date={post.Date} excerpt={post.Excerpt}/>
        {/each}
    </div>
</div>
</body>
